  "slug": "intestinal-liver-mice-0dd6",
  "summary": "Pre-treatment scRNA-seq, methylation and immune-state models now target toxicity, survival and response, alongside new glioblastoma plasticity maps.",
  "synthesis": "The main thread links molecular profiles to clinical endpoints. irAEGIS uses a pathway-guided, interpretable hierarchical model on pre-treatment scRNA-seq to predict immune-related adverse event risk, outperforming seven comparators. MANTIS trains a neural network on genome-wide DNA methylation from 2,786 patients to predict time-dependent survival and treatment effects in childhood brain tumors. Genialis reports that a biology-first model of tumor immune state predicts immunotherapy response on par with outcome-trained signatures. CALM provides an AML single-cell and bulk atlas with clinical annotations. A second strand addresses glioblastoma dynamics across scales. scDORI infers enhancer-driven GRNs from single-nucleus multiome data to decode plasticity, GlioTrace tracks single-cell invasion phenotypes ex vivo, and a reaction-diffusion model estimates the migration-to-proliferation ratio from single time-point MRI. A third strand focuses on clonal inference. LOTUS applies lineage-aware unbalanced optimal transport to barcoded scRNA-seq, CloneVI links mitochondrial genotype clones to cell state, and OncoSpot simulates spatial data with known subclones and CNAs for benchmarking.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-06"
}
